# {{SLUG}} — AWA skill for {{DOMAIN}}

An **Agentic Web Actions (AWA)** skill: a JavaScript module that exposes action
handlers an agent can dispatch against `{{DOMAIN}}`.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `manifest.json` | Marketplace + runtime metadata: `domain`, `slug`, `title`, `version`, `readme`, `actions`, `capabilities`, `urls`, `timeout`, `memoryLimitMB`. `mpx publish` ships this. |
| `skill.js` | Handler implementations (`module.exports = { manifest, handlers }`). |
| `GUIDE.md` | `$awa.*` API reference, manifest field table, and the metadata / README update checklist. |

## Quick start

```bash
mpx web up                              # start worker + GCS (auto-pulls images)
mpx web seed {{SLUG}}                   # upload this skill for local testing
mpx web session start {{SLUG}} --robot <uuid>   # dispatch actions
mpx publish .                           # publish v{{VERSION}} to the marketplace
```

Inspect the published metadata at any time:

```bash
mpx web readme <username>~{{SLUG}}
```

## Before you publish

1. Implement the handlers in `skill.js` and keep the `actions` docs in
   `manifest.json` matching them — the agent dispatches from those docs.
2. Update `capabilities` and `urls` to match what the skill actually reaches.
3. Update this README and `GUIDE.md` prose if behavior changed.
4. Bump `version` in `manifest.json` (or run `mpx web update-manifest .`).
5. `mpx publish .`

See the last section of `GUIDE.md` — **"Updating this README and the manifest
metadata"** — for the full field table and the shared `update-manifest` editor.
